=== artemis
--- art -D
-Dbam=	BAM, CRAM, VCF or BCF files (,-separated; bam1=, bam2=: in separate panels)
-DbamClone=	open the BAM files in N panels
-Dblack_belt_mode=	keep warnings to a minimum
-Dchado=	a Chado database (host:port/db?user)
-Dloguserplot=	userplot files, of log(data)
-Doffset=	the base position to open at
-Dread_only 	open the Chado database read-only
-Dshow_cov_plot 	open the coverage plot in BamView
-Dshow_forward_lines=	show the forward frame lines
-Dshow_reverse_lines=	show the reverse frame lines
-Dshow_snp_plot 	open the SNP plot in BamView
-Dshow_snps 	show SNP marks in BamView
-Duserplot=	userplot files (,-separated)
--- art -Dbam=reads.bam,
-Dbam=reads.bam,aln.fa 
-Dbam=reads.bam,genome.gbk 
-Dbam=reads.bam,gui_viewers.sh 
-Dbam=reads.bam,net.sif 
-Dbam=reads.bam,old.cys.bak 
-Dbam=reads.bam,reads.bam 
-Dbam=reads.bam,reads.cram 
-Dbam=reads.bam,script.txt 
-Dbam=reads.bam,sessions/
-Dbam=reads.bam,style.xml 
-Dbam=reads.bam,tree.nwk 
--- art -Dshow_forward_lines=
-Dshow_forward_lines=false 
-Dshow_forward_lines=true 
--- art genome.gbk +
+aln.fa 
+genome.gbk 
+gui_viewers.sh 
+net.sif 
+old.cys.bak 
+reads.bam 
+reads.cram 
+script.txt 
+sessions/
+style.xml 
+tree.nwk 
--- act -
-chado 	connect to a Chado database ($PGHOST, $PGPORT, $PGDATABASE, $PGUSER)
-h 	show the help
-help 	show the help
-options 	read options from a file
-quiet 	don't print the arguments Java is started with
--- bamview -a 
reads.bam 
reads.cram 
sessions/
--- bamview -v 
C 	coverage
IS 	inferred size
PS 	paired stack
S 	stack
ST 	strand
--- dnaplotter -t 
aln.fa 
genome.gbk 
gui_viewers.sh 
net.sif 
old.cys.bak 
reads.bam 
reads.cram 
script.txt 
sessions/
style.xml 
tree.nwk 
=== BandageNG
--- BandageNG 
image 	generate an image file of a graph
info 	display information about a graph
layout 	layout the graph
load 	launch the BandageNG GUI and load a graph file
querypaths 	output graph paths for BLAST queries
reduce 	save a subgraph of a larger graph
--- BandageNG image 
aln.fa 
graph.gfa 
sessions/
--- BandageNG image graph.gfa out.png --sco
--scope=	the graph's scope
--- BandageNG image graph.gfa out.png --colour 
csv 
custom 
depth 
gc 
gfa 
random 
uniform 
--- BandageNG querypaths graph.gfa 
aln.fa 
sessions/
=== pymol, chimerax, vmd
--- pymol -A 
1 	simple viewer window
3 	internal GUI only, no splash
4 	used by PYMOLVIEWER
5 	helper application
6 	full screen presentation
--- pymol -r 
sessions/
--- chimerax --start
--start_tool=	start a tool at startup
--- vmd -dispdev 
cave 
none 
text 
win 
--- vmd -ps
-psf 	load a PSF file
